        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "ef122d32-cdcc-55fe-b851-5caafc507dba",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Kingdom of Slavonia, Slavonian Military Frontier, Military Frontier, Milan\n- Organizations: Habsburg Monarchy, Austrian Empire, Austro-Hungarian Empire, Jesuits\n- People: Tomo Zdelarić, Ludovico Luigi Carlo Maria di Barbiano di Belgiojoso\n- Roles: Austrian diplomat, Lieutenant Field Marshal\n\nFacts:\n- The Kingdom of Slavonia was a province of the Habsburg Monarchy and later the Austrian Empire from 1699 to 1868.\n- The southern parts of the Kingdom of Slavonia were part of the Slavonian Military Frontier, which was a section of the Military Frontier.\n- The Military Frontier was a province along the southern borderland of the Habsburg Monarchy and later the Austrian and Austro-Hungarian Empire.\n- Tomo Zdelarić, who lived circa 1531 to 8 April 1572, was the earliest Jesuit from the Habsburg Kingdom of Slavonia.\n- Ludovico Luigi Carlo Maria di Barbiano di Belgiojoso, also known as Ludwig Karl Maria von Barbiano Graf von Belgiojoso, lived from 2 January 1728 to 15 May 1801 and served the Habsburg Monarchy in the second half of the 18th century as an Austrian diplomat and Lieutenant Field Marshal.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "fa7bdf9e-a31e-5443-af99-a349b94cdf01",
        "text": "Page: Kingdom of Slavonia. Sentence: The Kingdom of Slavonia (Croatian: \"Kraljevina Slavonija\" ; German: \"Königreich Slawonien\" ; Latin: \"Regnum Sclavoniae\" ; Hungarian: \"Szlavón Királyság\" ) was a province of the Habsburg Monarchy and the Austrian Empire that existed from 1699 to 1868.\nPage: Kingdom of Slavonia. Sentence: The southern parts of these regions were part of the Slavonian Military Frontier, which was a section of the Military Frontier.\nPage: Military Frontier. Sentence: The Military Frontier was a province straddling the southern borderland of the Habsburg Monarchy and later the Austrian and Austro-Hungarian Empire.\nPage: Tomo Zdelarić. Sentence: Tomo Zdelarić () (c. 1531 – 8 April 1572} was the earliest Jesuit from Habsburg Kingdom of Slavonia.\nPage: Ludovico, Count di Belgiojoso. Sentence: Ludovico Luigi Carlo Maria di Barbiano di Belgiojoso or Ludwig Karl Maria von Barbiano Graf von Belgiojoso (2 January 1728 – 15 May 1801, Milan) was an Austrian diplomat and Lieutenant Field Marshal who served the Habsburg Monarchy in the second half of the 18th century.",
